  "caveats": [
    "Both data heaps are resident CPU-visible system memory; allocations are separate.",
    "ISA placement, cache policy, state programming and native wait implementation differ.",
    "Native wait uses an OS event on WDDM and the driver's fence wait on L0.",
    "Hybrid budgets 50/100 us after submit, checked every 32 polls; OS scheduling can extend wall time.",
    "Thread cycles include timer/counter overhead and are CPU execution cost, not wall time or a power measurement.",
    "Poll uses pause loops with bounded completion checks on both backends.",
    "Native-wait calls count fallback invocation, not confirmed OS blocking or context switches.",
    "Wait-policy medians come from separate processes; per-policy comparisons are observations, not direct A/B/A policy pairs.",
    "CPU-cycle counters are collected outside wall-clock timing; their interval includes timer/counter overhead.",
    "Only the calling thread is counted; driver/background threads and total system CPU use are not measured.",
    "These workloads use no scratch/private memory and do not establish full-model speedup.",
    "No production wait policy has been changed."
  ],
